[ ] Retire the homed Darrion account =retire-homed $Erased and verified 2026-10-21 (see Log). Left: drop the stale Darrion entry from group data (sudo gpasswd -d Darrion data), remove that account's ssh key from GitHub if it was added, and unlink that desktop in Signal. The drive stays in its enclosure until =desktop-install moves it.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:04 <homed-inventory #01a15bc6-5a28-7232-9260-740b2519e82d
[ ] Sort the desktop's software into layers or drop =desktop-sort $The 164 unlisted packages plus user level (Flatpaks, user units, ~/.local, the AUR set), each into one row of the layer table or drop. The facilitator drafts it grouped by purpose; Darrion makes the calls. Docker, docker-compose and podman are proposed drops.$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 #01a15bc6-5a30-7963-875a-79fd55448791
[ ] Decide where the desktop package list lives =desktop-list-home $NEEDS DECISION: A, chezmoi packages.yaml installs on today's Arch desktop and moves to personal-os later; B, a personal-os desktop profile (not yet booted) is the list now and today's desktop installs from it, so the image is the inventory. On personal-os /usr is read-only, so a chezmoi pacman installer has no future there.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:04 #01a15bc6-5a38-7f61-a121-7d3281a2af35
[ ] Write the desktop mkosi profile =desktop-profile $Base plus hardware selection (Intel and NVIDIA), from the sort. Built and booted in a VM before it touches hardware.$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 <desktop-sort <desktop-list-home #01a15bc6-5a3f-7a32-b39e-7e9bf807954e
[ ] Mount /home and /data from their own disks =desktop-mounts $repart lays out only the boot disk; the other two become mount units. /data keeps group data, setgid and default ACLs.$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 <desktop-profile #01a15bc6-5a48-75d1-a68b-cb281ca65d2c
[ ] Install the desktop profile on the 1 TB NVMe beside Arch =desktop-install $Darrion, 2026-10-21: install while the drive is still in its USB enclosure, then move it. 1) Test the built image in a VM from the image file. 2) Write it to the drive from Arch, addressed as /dev/disk/by-id/usb-Best_Buy_NS-PCNVMEHDE_-C__4834500000003539-0:0, confirmed before writing (four NVMe disks once it is inside). 3) Boot the desktop from the USB drive once. 4) Move it into the free M.2 slot (a standard M.2 NVMe; the desktop has no SATA disks to lose) and boot from there. Arch stays untouched; the boot menu picks. Secure Boot is already on with Darrion's own keys (bootctl: enabled (user), likely sbctl): either add personal-os's db certificate beside them or sign the desktop image with the sbctl keys; decide at this step.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:20 <desktop-profile <retire-homed #01a15bd4-c3df-7782-bc59-31be2e0f11a2
[ ] Wipe the Arch root disk once personal-os holds up =wipe-arch $nvme2n1 (WD_BLACK SN850X) is freed for data. What holds up means is agreed with Darrion before the wipe; the wipe is a disk write that needs Darrion's explicit go.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:20 <desktop-install #01a15bd4-c3e8-7d72-91f4-8697fb1281c2
